  "_authoring_notes": "Gold-standard expected output for Path D against the manufacturing-products-with-policies fixture. Authored by Claude Code; reviewed by user at Stop 0 PAUSE #1 (2026-05-09). First fixture exercising aggregation-derived mappings (CategoryName from DISTINCT ProductGroupName) and constant-value mappings (BusinessUnit / SourceSystem / BusinessSegment with empty source_field_ids). decision_type values use the canonical vocabulary from PR 109. 1 inferred_target for vendors (PreferredVendor has no target home). [Stop 0 PAUSE #1 corrections, 2026-05-09] Q1 applied: Categories.CategoryID (c4...020) flipped from coverage `gap` to `covered`, and a 14th mapping added with empty source_field_ids + combination_type custom_sql to represent the system-generated PK with a default_value_recommendation in coverage. Rationale: a system-generated PK is `covered` with a generation strategy, not `gap` (which means \"unknown how to fill\"). Q2 applied: StandardCost (c4...004) mapping combination_type changed from `single` to `custom_sql`. Rationale: the model folds negative-cost sanitization (CASE WHEN UnitCost < 0 THEN NULL) into combination_sql; that is strictly more correct than treating DQ-cleanup as a separate concern. Both corrections align the fixture to Path D's strictly-more-correct interpretation rather than testing aspirational fixture choices. Naming-axis mismatches on lookup_recall (model: `product_group_casing_normalization`, fixture: `product_group_to_category`) and inferred_targets_recall (model: `Vendors / PreferredVendor relationship`, fixture: `vendors`) intentionally LEFT MISALIGNED — they are the iter-2 Stop 1 target (canonical naming vocabulary for lookups + inferred_targets, mirroring iter-1's decision_type vocabulary fix).",
